{"content":{"activity_type":"event_msg/task_complete","completed_at":1790216317,"duration_ms":161362,"last_agent_message":"## Project snapshot\n\nConversation Ledger is a Node 20+/TypeScript CLI and library that captures coding-agent transcripts, normalizes them into provenance-rich events, and stores them as append-only Git notes.\n\nThe main flow is:\n\n`CLI hooks/manual capture → source adapters → normalized event schema → annals storage → git-notes transport`\n\nThe repository now owns the conversation vocabulary, five adapters, installation, and CLI presentation. The extracted `annals` package owns most storage, Git, redaction, review, re-anchoring, and transport mechanics; the thin boundary is visible in [ledger.ts](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/src/ledger.ts:10) and [store.ts](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/src/store.ts:46).\n\nCurrent state:\n\n- Version `0.26.0`.\n- Supported adapters: Claude Code, Codex, opencode, Gemini CLI, and Qwen Code.\n- Clean worktree on `cleanup/remove-migration-tooling`.\n- Branch is one commit ahead of `main`, removing the completed one-time ev1 migration script, tests, and documentation.\n- `npm test`: **90 passed, 0 failed**.\n- No skipped or TODO tests.\n- No source-level `TODO`/`FIXME` markers beyond documented deferred work.\n\n## Most actionable remaining work\n\n1. **Complete Codex subagent discovery.** Child rollouts are normalized correctly, but capture does not follow `sub_agent_activity.agent_thread_id` to locate them. Children are therefore captured only when something independently hands cledger their rollout. See [README.md](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/README.md:1014).\n\n2. **Close transcript-tail gaps.** Claude and Qwen sweep previously tracked sessions on a later hook, but a repository’s final session can retain uncaptured closing lines. Claude also lacks an intentional `capture claude-code --all` backfill path. See [README.md](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/README.md:1025).\n\n3. **Test and expose the opencode fallback.** If opencode renames its hook session-ID field, cledger falls back to the most recently updated session. That path is untested and currently silent; the roadmap calls for a direct test and warning. See [README.md](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/README.md:513).\n\n4. **Replace plaintext known-secret storage with hashes.** This is the clearest remaining security improvement. The proposed design uses salted, length-indexed digests and candidate scanning, avoiding a readable aggregation of confirmed secrets. See [README.md](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/README.md:801) and [README.md](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/README.md:815).\n\n5. **Stop routine scan output from feeding back into captured conversations.** The proposed behavior is to print a count and safe inspection instructions by default, while preserving an explicit CI reporting mode. See [README.md](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/README.md:554).\n\n6. **Automate re-normalization after adapter upgrades.** Raw unknown events can already be upgraded safely and idempotently, but only through `cledger renormalize`; detecting an adapter-version transition and triggering it remains deferred. See [renormalize.ts](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/src/renormalize.ts:27).\n\n## Documentation cleanup found\n\nSeveral references were missed during the `annals` extraction:\n\n- [CLAUDE.md](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/CLAUDE.md:16) points to secret-corpus and redaction tests that no longer exist here.\n- [README.md](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/README.md:267) has the same stale fixture reference.\n- README and technical design still say the forge implementation lives in `src/forge/`, although it now comes from `annals`: [README.md](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/README.md:962), [WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:698).\n- The historical reasoning roadmap says embedded Codex ciphertext is still dropped, contradicting both current implementation and product intent. It is now preserved as a sealed sibling event: [README.md](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/README.md:949), [codex.ts](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/src/adapters/codex.ts:288).\n\n## Release hygiene\n\nTwo issues matter before npm publication:\n\n- `annals` remains a sibling-file dependency, `\"annals\": \"file:../annals\"`, so a published package would not install normally for consumers. See [package.json](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/package.json:52).\n- The build does not clean `dist`. A package dry run from this checkout includes obsolete compiled modules such as `dist/forge`, `dist/canonical`, and the old redaction implementation. A fresh checkout would avoid this, but a clean-output step should be added before build/package. See [package.json](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/package.json:42).\n\n## Longer-term backlog\n\nThe roadmap also retains:\n\n- New adapters: Kimi CLI, Antigravity, Copilot CLI, Factory Droid, Cursor, aider, Goose/Amp.\n- Path-based capture exclusion.\n- Post-push purge coordination.\n- Multi-remote/fork-aware fetch staging.\n- Richer conversation context in `cledger review`.\n- Better false-positive discrimination.\n- Gemini source-version provenance and live verification of several Qwen shapes.\n- Sub-turn citation anchors.\n- Forge PR/MR conversation capture and CI/App integration.\n- Optional file-snapshot bodies.\n- Harness-artifact/document capture.\n- Re-anchor’s accepted already-dead-branch cursor gap.\n- A possible explicit conversation manifest.\n\nMy suggested order is: merge the current cleanup branch, fix the stale docs and packaging, then tackle Codex child discovery and transcript-tail completeness. Those are the most concrete gaps between the product’s “whole record” promise and present capture behavior.","started_at":1790216156,"time_to_first_token_ms":1379,"turn_id":"01a0d132-b4b9-7b20-9b60-b53aa8fb7ec3"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"473ad0ff2f5a839e9a29cb9a5c2d5e247c1801e0","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"id":"ev2-5b4fe4e606b0405a2a63b5dfde48bc9d79e44b67894a975dc2ed3859d7e82fd6","kind":"activity","meta":{"actor":{"type":"agent"},"model":"gpt-5.6-sol","provider":"openai","session_id":"01a0d132-3af5-7f63-9ce8-f92787b93442","source":"codex","source_version":"0.156.1"},"occurred_at":"2026-09-24T02:18:37.713Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.26.0"},"raw":{"data":{"ordinal":152,"payload":{"completed_at":1790216317,"duration_ms":161362,"last_agent_message":"## Project snapshot\n\nConversation Ledger is a Node 20+/TypeScript CLI and library that captures coding-agent transcripts, normalizes them into provenance-rich events, and stores them as append-only Git notes.\n\nThe main flow is:\n\n`CLI hooks/manual capture → source adapters → normalized event schema → annals storage → git-notes transport`\n\nThe repository now owns the conversation vocabulary, five adapters, installation, and CLI presentation. The extracted `annals` package owns most storage, Git, redaction, review, re-anchoring, and transport mechanics; the thin boundary is visible in [ledger.ts](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/src/ledger.ts:10) and [store.ts](/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/src/store.ts:46).\n\nCurrent state:\n\n- Version `0.26.0`.\n- Supported adapters: Claude Code, Codex, opencode, Gemini CLI, and Qwen Code.\n- Clean worktree on `cleanup/remove-migration-tooling`.\n- Branch is one commit ahead of `main`, removing 