{"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"Implemented, reviewed, and merged the clearly scoped work. Both repositories have no open PRs, and the shared checkout is clean on `main`.\n\nMerged:\n\n- [cledger #16](https://github.com/evintunador/conversation-ledger/pull/16) — opencode fallback warning and integration coverage.\n- [cledger #17](https://github.com/evintunador/conversation-ledger/pull/17) — post-Annals documentation drift.\n- [cledger #18](https://github.com/evintunador/conversation-ledger/pull/18) — recursive Codex subagent discovery.\n- [cledger #19](https://github.com/evintunador/conversation-ledger/pull/19) — explicit `capture claude-code --all`.\n- [annals #1](https://github.com/evintunador/annals/pull/1) — salted-digest known-secret storage.\n- [cledger #20](https://github.com/evintunador/conversation-ledger/pull/20) — corresponding docs and Annals API compatibility.\n\nEvery PR received an independent adversarial review before merging. Those reviews caught several substantive issues, including changed Codex record shapes, discarded opencode warnings, Claude’s project-directory override, recoverable secret-probe data, concurrent-write loss, Unicode mismatches, and a stale-lock race.\n\nFinal clean-clone verification:\n\n- Conversation Ledger: **99/99 passing**\n- Annals: **158 passing, 1 optional gitleaks test skipped**\n- No open PRs\n- Local checkout: `main...origin/main`, clean\n\nOn item 5: not quite already done. Reports no longer print matched content or context, so the direct re-seeding problem is fixed. They still print each finding’s fingerprint and coordinates by default. The proposed “count plus inspection pointer by default, explicit detailed report for CI” behavior remains unimplemented, and the roadmap correctly identifies the unresolved terminal-versus-CI policy choice.\n\nPublication work was deliberately untouched.\n\nWhat remains is predominantly the judgment/live-validation backlog:\n\n- Scan reporting policy from item 5.\n- Final-session tai